harnessloop/plugins/harnessloop/skills/harnessloop-loop/SKILL.md:468:- `loop_autocontinue_anomaly` / `loop_anomaly_skipped_unparsable` — loop-autocontinue anomaly gate (batch 3 of the same spec, §4/§5, restated by that spec's Appendix B.1/B.2/F.3; see `check_loop_autocontinue_anomaly`). Project-level, not per-round: computed once per run from `.harnessloop/state/control-contract.md`'s three canonical fields (`- Profile:`, `- Auto-continue on positive:`, `- Auto-continue on negative/neutral remediation:` — parsed the same `- <label>:` / `_uncoded_lines` way as every other field in this file) and `.harnessloop/state/evidence-index.md`'s table, then evaluated once per goal against only that goal's *latest* round (highest integer round-directory name — being latest already means no successor round exists yet, so post-Appendix-F this needs no `continued:`-shaped field of its own; see Appendix F.3). Reports one `loop_autocontinue_anomaly` when **all** of: `- Profile:` is `lite` or `standard` (`strict`/`custom` excluded); `- Auto-continue on positive: yes`; that round's `- Feedback:` normalizes to `positive`; and every data row of `evidence-index.md` has `Artifact health` = `valid`. **Polarity is deliberately conservative — fail-closed toward *silence*, the opposite of every other fail-closed rule in this file**: when any one condition cannot be mechanically determined at all (a field never written, a value that does not normalize, `evidence-index.md` missing, or its table unparsable), the anomaly is **not** reported; unless some *other* condition is already determinately `False` (three-valued/Kleene AND — a known `False` beats an unknown), it is instead counted in `loop_anomaly_skipped_unparsable`, so "this could not be judged" stays visible instead of collapsing into an ordinary non-trigger. **This is never a violation and never changes the exit code** (§4.2: promoting it to a hard gate needs its own predegistration and pilot, same discipline as the loop-continuation record gate above never judging a stop reason's honesty). Appendix B.1 pairs it with exactly one real violation, `loop-contract-profile-missing`: once a project is "activated" (any round anywhere in it has ever declared `- Loop continuation:` **or** `- Predecessor:` — Appendix F folded the latter in, since that is the field a fresh round actually writes post-reversal), a `control-contract.md` with no `- Profile:` field at all is fail-closed red, because an unwritten field would otherwise be a switch held entirely by the party this gate checks (it silently guarantees the anomaly can never fire). Before activation, a missing `Profile:` field has zero effect.
harnessloop/plugins/harnessloop/skills/harnessloop-loop/SKILL.md:522:- **The conservative/fail-closed polarity itself is a switch the audited party holds open.** Writing `evidence-index.md` (or any of the three canonical `control-contract.md` fields) in a shape this gate cannot parse makes `loop_anomaly_skipped_unparsable` absorb what would otherwise have been a reported anomaly — indistinguishable at the coverage level from an honest parsing gap. Appendix B.1 (`loop-contract-profile-missing`) closes exactly one instance of this (a wholly absent `Profile:` field, once activated); it does not close the general case, and this is registered here rather than silently declared solved.
